  "agent_inheritance": "An agent acting for a human is evaluated against BOTH sides. The human side is the human's own role and human bindings, with the same no-rule fallback a human gets. The agent side is the rules bound to agent:<app>:<agentId> or to the app wildcard agent:<app>:*. A deny from either side denies, so a per-agent deny beats the wildcard, and an approval requirement from either side applies. Agents hold no standing rights of their own: an app with no agent binding (DeepSignal today) is refused everything. The nessie app is seeded with an unconditioned agent:nessie:* allow for every pair the code requests, so a Nessie agent may do exactly what the person it acts for may do; which tools the agent holds at all is Nessie's grant.",
  "notes_compliance": "record.erase: owner-only and still approval-gated (a second person confirms; single-owner teams fall back to the same owner confirming through the elicitation — the audit trail is the control). suppression.create is member-open on purpose: recording an objection must never be blocked. suppression.admin (= remove) is owner + approval."
}
